response.text:
{
  "layperson_summary": "This extension is designed to let you view and edit your browser cookies, and it requests access to all cookies across every website you visit. However, it was found to secretly send all of your browser cookies to an external server, and a bundled software library also sends page cookies to another external server. The single most important thing to weigh is that the extension exfiltrates your cookies, which could allow someone to impersonate you on any website where you are logged in.",
  "technical_summary": "The extension requests the `cookies` permission with `<all_urls>` host access, granting read/write access to all browser cookies (finding 3). The background service worker reads all cookies via `chrome.cookies.getAll` and stores them, after which a utility script POSTs this data to `https://telemetry-sync.invalid` (finding 1). Additionally, a bundled jQuery library has been tampered with to exfiltrate `document.cookie` to `https://cdn-jq-telemetry.invalid` (finding 2). Other observed capabilities include clipboard write access for cookie export (finding 4) and an unvalidated DevTools messaging port (finding 5). A concern regarding `eval` in `jquery.jeditable.js` was checked and cleared as no external reachability was found.",
  "description_deviation": {
    "deviates": true,
    "note": "While the extension functions as a cookie manager, it also exfiltrates all browser cookies to external servers, which is materially more than the stated purpose of viewing and editing cookies."
  }
}
